(5791741, 840800, 16197, '<td valign="top">Interesting image, it is nice to see the building through the snow.  However overall it does not pop enough to give me shivers.  The contrasts are nice.  Just something extra missing.</td>', 'Interesting image, it is nice to see the building through the snow.  However overall it does not pop enough to give me shivers.  The contrasts are nice.  Just something extra missing.', '2010-01-02 17:54:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791744, 840793, 16197, '<td valign="top">This is a fun image and I am surprised the title does not have the word key in it.  Yet even though this is a fun find, there is a lot of noise/texture that distracts throughout the image.  It does not give me enough pop nor emotion.  But still a nice find.</td>', 'This is a fun image and I am surprised the title does not have the word key in it.  Yet even though this is a fun find, there is a lot of noise/texture that distracts throughout the image.  It does not give me enough pop nor emotion.  But still a nice find.', '2010-01-02 17:55:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791746, 842204, 16197, '<td valign="top">This is a nice lighting image, though I believe there is too much white-space at the top of the image.  A tighter closer crop to the lighting and where there is the most interest may have made this a stronger overall image.</td>', 'This is a nice lighting image, though I believe there is too much white-space at the top of the image.  A tighter closer crop to the lighting and where there is the most interest may have made this a stronger overall image.', '2010-01-02 17:56:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791752, 843316, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like the stark editing here, the blown walls work very well indeed and you have communicated the height of the building very well. I like how the textures have been brought out too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: not too much, I like it as it is.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image which benefits from a well crafted edit and a great POV.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I really like the stark editing here, the blown walls work very well indeed and you have communicated the height of the building very well. I like how the textures have been brought out too. Critical stuff: not too much, I like it as it is. Overall: A very effective image which benefits from a well crafted edit and a great POV.', '2010-01-02 18:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791763, 843353, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I think the tilt really works here, especially with the placement of the rail in the bottom left corner. I quite like the coloration too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the softness / glow in the image is perhaps a little overdone.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting picture but one that is perhaps a little over-edited.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I think the tilt really works here, especially with the placement of the rail in the bottom left corner. I quite like the coloration too. Critical stuff: I think the softness / glow in the image is perhaps a little overdone. Overall: An interesting picture but one that is perhaps a little over-edited.', '2010-01-02 18:07:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791779, 842894, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: There''s lots to look at here and the the light is very interesting. I really like the moon too. The road has an interesting quality to it.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the intrinsic interest in the scene might fall short of that needed to please the voters.<br/> <br/>Overall: A nice image which benefits from a sympathetic edit but one which in the final analysis may not have enough to give.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: There''s lots to look at here and the the light is very interesting. I really like the moon too. The road has an interesting quality to it. Critical stuff: I think the intrinsic interest in the scene might fall short of that needed to please the voters. Overall: A nice image which benefits from a sympathetic edit but one which in the final analysis may not have enough to give.', '2010-01-02 18:17:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791780, 842926, 103759, '<td valign="top">nice photo...jackie sure is cute.... although, I think he is wanting a new sheep for you making him do this shot...</td>', 'nice photo...jackie sure is cute.... although, I think he is wanting a new sheep for you making him do this shot...', '2010-01-02 18:17:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791790, 841454, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: This funny and really well executed too. I like the way Santa and Mrs seem t be completely unfazed! Could that child be crying any harder??<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I can see why you did it but a monochrome santa does seem to lack something.<br/> <br/>Overall: A great candid shot - well made.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: This funny and really well executed too. I like the way Santa and Mrs seem t be completely unfazed! Could that child be crying any harder?? Critical stuff: I can see why you did it but a monochrome santa does seem to lack something. Overall: A great candid shot - well made.', '2010-01-02 18:25:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791795, 839075, 16197, '<td valign="top">nice clean classic portrait.  Maybe even commercial.  Having the model against the wall/ground is a nice touch as well as the camera angle being above the eye.  The contrasts are nice and upon second view I am going to bump the score a bit (which I rarely do).</td>', 'nice clean classic portrait.  Maybe even commercial.  Having the model against the wall/ground is a nice touch as well as the camera angle being above the eye.  The contrasts are nice and upon second view I am going to bump the score a bit (which I rarely do).', '2010-01-02 18:30:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791797, 843009, 16197, '<td valign="top">Nice simple image.  There is some motion blur on the prairie grass which causes distraction but the trees all seem to be in focus.  The clouds are kinda interesting.  Though if this image was pushed a bit, make the colours pop and the contrasts scream it would be really fantastic.</td>', 'Nice simple image.  There is some motion blur on the prairie grass which causes distraction but the trees all seem to be in focus.  The clouds are kinda interesting.  Though if this image was pushed a bit, make the colours pop and the contrasts scream it would be really fantastic.', '2010-01-02 18:31:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791799, 842956, 16197, '<td valign="top">Nice simple image however the thin top/bottom border has to go.  Being so thin and only on the top/bottom it adds nothing and only takes away from the image.  However there really is nothing spectacular about this image, the interest lays mostly in the gradual colour fade as well as the disruption in the water.</td>', 'Nice simple image however the thin top/bottom border has to go.  Being so thin and only on the top/bottom it adds nothing and only takes away from the image.  However there really is nothing spectacular about this image, the interest lays mostly in the gradual colour fade as well as the disruption in the water.', '2010-01-02 18:32:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791800, 840994, 16197, '<td valign="top">This image offers something but does not quite hand it over.  There are many great elements here from the dramatic nature of the clouds to the drama of the water paths on land.  The hint of great colour lays hidden within muted tones.  There is hope here... but not just there.</td>', 'This image offers something but does not quite hand it over.  There are many great elements here from the dramatic nature of the clouds to the drama of the water paths on land.  The hint of great colour lays hidden within muted tones.  There is hope here... but not just there.', '2010-01-02 18:33:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791801, 842623, 16197, '<td valign="top">Nice working portrait.  However for me I would have liked camera angle to move to the right a bit.  To bring in more of the front and less side.  This would also or I should hope also get rid of the truck which is a distraction.  Focus more on the worker and what they are doing, which includes their background which may be cords, or other items to iron and such.</td>', 'Nice working portrait.  However for me I would have liked camera angle to move to the right a bit.  To bring in more of the front and less side.  This would also or I should hope also get rid of the truck which is a distraction.  Focus more on the worker and what they are doing, which includes their background which may be cords, or other items to iron and such.', '2010-01-02 18:35:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791802, 840238, 16197, '<td valign="top">Simple clean portrait I am sure the model is extremely happy with.  Though for this type of challenge it does not offer enough for me to give it two looks.  Sure its clean, lighting is nice, and the colours work.  Just nothing behind it.</td>', 'Simple clean portrait I am sure the model is extremely happy with.  Though for this type of challenge it does not offer enough for me to give it two looks.  Sure its clean, lighting is nice, and the colours work.  Just nothing behind it.', '2010-01-02 18:36:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791806, 841145, 16197, '<td valign="top">A cute portrait, though with the wrinkled sheet and the bright highlight on the side of her hair it causes a distraction.  Also being a simple cute portrait may be nice for normal settings or for personal use however for a free study I feel it just does not give me enough.  No drama or pop.  Also the clarity could be sharper and the depth more recognizable.</td>', 'A cute portrait, though with the wrinkled sheet and the bright highlight on the side of her hair it causes a distraction.  Also being a simple cute portrait may be nice for normal settings or for personal use however for a free study I feel it just does not give me enough.  No drama or pop.  Also the clarity could be sharper and the depth more recognizable.', '2010-01-02 18:37:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791810, 842812, 16197, '<td valign="top">Interesting image.  Not quite sure what I think of it but I do know it does not blow me out of the water.  Im assuming this is a negative b/w maybe even a bit of solarization or something.  Maybe not.  Im sure it has its place but for here it is not quite.</td>', 'Interesting image.  Not quite sure what I think of it but I do know it does not blow me out of the water.  Im assuming this is a negative b/w maybe even a bit of solarization or something.  Maybe not.  Im sure it has its place but for here it is not quite.', '2010-01-02 18:38:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791816, 842854, 16197, '<td valign="top">I read the title and you completely lose me.  Not that it had much to go on in the first place.  There should be more contrast or at least a highlight along the hat so the viewer doesn''t lose it into the background.   It appears to be direct light which loses any depth of character.    .... The Vamp.  I would like to ask what here makes you see ''vamp''? Though I also need to ask what do you think a ''vamp'' is?  No judgment on the model, Or attacks, just observation of character portrayed within the image... The Tramp, may be a better title.  More believable because of the wardrobe choice.  Remember this has nothing to do with the model personally, only the visual of the image in front of me.</td>', 'I read the title and you completely lose me.  Not that it had much to go on in the first place.  There should be more contrast or at least a highlight along the hat so the viewer doesn''t lose it into the background.   It appears to be direct light which loses any depth of character.    .... The Vamp.  I would like to ask what here makes you see ''vamp''? Though I also need to ask what do you think a ''vamp'' is?  No judgment on the model, Or attacks, just observation of character portrayed within the image... The Tramp, may be a better title.  More believable because of the wardrobe choice.  Remember this has nothing to do with the model personally, only the visual of the image in front of me.', '2010-01-02 18:41:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5791817, 842924, 76335, '<td valign="top">I like the green tones, but otherwise the composition adds nothing new to an all-too-familiar set up.</td>', 'I like the green tones, but otherwise the composition adds nothing new to an all-too-familiar set up.', '2010-01-02 18:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
