(5792335, 838946, 23317, '<td valign="top">So simple.  Nice softness.  In my top 5.</td>', 'So simple.  Nice softness.  In my top 5.', '2010-01-02 23:25:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792336, 841497, 23317, '<td valign="top">Excellent saturation.  My of my two 10s.</td>', 'Excellent saturation.  My of my two 10s.', '2010-01-02 23:25:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792342, 842995, 42100, '<td valign="top">Beautiful sky with those wispy and rippled clouds...great highlighting on that home as well.  Very nice photo!</td>', 'Beautiful sky with those wispy and rippled clouds...great highlighting on that home as well.  Very nice photo!', '2010-01-02 23:28:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792344, 843234, 42100, '<td valign="top">Ha, that''s one experienced and talented little mooch!  Hope you threw a few peanuts his way!  :)</td>', 'Ha, that''s one experienced and talented little mooch!  Hope you threw a few peanuts his way!  :)', '2010-01-02 23:29:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792350, 842925, 42100, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot with the streaky trees and streaky falling snow...b&amp;w really works well for this!</td>', 'Very cool shot with the streaky trees and streaky falling snow...b&w really works well for this!', '2010-01-02 23:31:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792354, 842212, 42100, '<td valign="top">Great icy blue tones...really inflects the coldness of this scene!</td>', 'Great icy blue tones...really inflects the coldness of this scene!', '2010-01-02 23:33:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792358, 842838, 42100, '<td valign="top">The suggestiveness of this says much more, than a more in your face approach would...like the grain for this as well.</td>', 'The suggestiveness of this says much more, than a more in your face approach would...like the grain for this as well.', '2010-01-02 23:35:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792362, 843087, 42100, '<td valign="top">This was a great choice for the panoramic crop and black borders...nice execution on this one all around!</td>', 'This was a great choice for the panoramic crop and black borders...nice execution on this one all around!', '2010-01-02 23:38:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792366, 843101, 42100, '<td valign="top">Cute pup...great clarity on him too!  Great job on showing the surrounding environment with losing the little guy in it.</td>', 'Cute pup...great clarity on him too!  Great job on showing the surrounding environment with losing the little guy in it.', '2010-01-02 23:40:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792372, 842210, 76335, '<td valign="top">Wonderful use of flare.</td>', 'Wonderful use of flare.', '2010-01-02 23:46:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792373, 842647, 105441, '<td valign="top">Great image, J!  Great framing, use of HDR.</td>', 'Great image, J!  Great framing, use of HDR.', '2010-01-02 23:46:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792376, 843174, 76335, '<td valign="top">Wish it were entirely in black and white. The pink background is too strong. Great idea anyway.</td>', 'Wish it were entirely in black and white. The pink background is too strong. Great idea anyway.', '2010-01-02 23:47:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792382, 843051, 42100, '<td valign="top">It''s like a blend of two worlds in this photo...with the crispy detail in the old station and canopy, and then the blur of the modern train.  The train portion is in a hurry much like modern life, while the passengers on the station side of the photo seem to be moving at a much more leisurely pace.  Great b&amp;w tones and photo!</td>', 'It''s like a blend of two worlds in this photo...with the crispy detail in the old station and canopy, and then the blur of the modern train.  The train portion is in a hurry much like modern life, while the passengers on the station side of the photo seem to be moving at a much more leisurely pace.  Great b&w tones and photo!', '2010-01-02 23:48:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792384, 842306, 105441, '<td valign="top">The softness, lack of contrast, and low saturation are an interesting effect, but I do not find it too interesting.  I do like the gulls focus on something off to camera right though.</td>', 'The softness, lack of contrast, and low saturation are an interesting effect, but I do not find it too interesting.  I do like the gulls focus on something off to camera right though.', '2010-01-02 23:49:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792386, 843221, 42100, '<td valign="top">Interesting dichotomy with what looks like a palace in the background and the trash and debris of the foreground.  Nice composition on this as well!</td>', 'Interesting dichotomy with what looks like a palace in the background and the trash and debris of the foreground.  Nice composition on this as well!', '2010-01-02 23:51:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792387, 840597, 105441, '<td valign="top">Great image and use of wireless flash.  The shadow across the bottom is distracting, though.</td>', 'Great image and use of wireless flash.  The shadow across the bottom is distracting, though.', '2010-01-02 23:51:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792388, 838147, 76335, '<td valign="top">Level that horizon!</td>', 'Level that horizon!', '2010-01-02 23:51:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792389, 843091, 105441, '<td valign="top">Nice processing.</td>', 'Nice processing.', '2010-01-02 23:51:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792392, 842162, 76335, '<td valign="top">The extreme angle isn''t doing much for me. Also would like to see her face a bit. The profile might be fine except for her fingers in the background...</td>', 'The extreme angle isn''t doing much for me. Also would like to see her face a bit. The profile might be fine except for her fingers in the background...', '2010-01-02 23:53:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792393, 843110, 105441, '<td valign="top">Great long exposure, will be interested in seeing if this is an HDR or if the rocks were lit.</td>', 'Great long exposure, will be interested in seeing if this is an HDR or if the rocks were lit.', '2010-01-02 23:53:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792394, 841434, 105441, '<td valign="top">Nice sky.</td>', 'Nice sky.', '2010-01-02 23:54:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792396, 843010, 76335, '<td valign="top">This is a photograph? Wow.</td>', 'This is a photograph? Wow.', '2010-01-02 23:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792398, 842946, 105441, '<td valign="top">Wow, can''t wait to see the author''s notes on how this was done.  Great result.</td>', 'Wow, can''t wait to see the author''s notes on how this was done.  Great result.', '2010-01-02 23:55:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792401, 841793, 105441, '<td valign="top">Nice light, great background.</td>', 'Nice light, great background.', '2010-01-02 23:57:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792404, 841733, 105441, '<td valign="top">Interesting use of selective color - I like it a lot.</td>', 'Interesting use of selective color - I like it a lot.', '2010-01-02 23:58:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792408, 842995, 105441, '<td valign="top">Excellent sky.</td>', 'Excellent sky.', '2010-01-02 23:59:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792413, 843161, 105441, '<td valign="top">Not quite sharp enough for my taste, but it is quite a capture.</td>', 'Not quite sharp enough for my taste, but it is quite a capture.', '2010-01-03 00:02:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792415, 841561, 105441, '<td valign="top">Excellent portrait and lighting.  I like the matching blue eyes.</td>', 'Excellent portrait and lighting.  I like the matching blue eyes.', '2010-01-03 00:02:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792421, 843350, 105441, '<td valign="top">Great portrait, but the vertical lines above his head, as well as clipping just the very top of his head, are a bit distracting.  The light and focus are excellent.</td>', 'Great portrait, but the vertical lines above his head, as well as clipping just the very top of his head, are a bit distracting.  The light and focus are excellent.', '2010-01-03 00:06:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792423, 843276, 16197, '<td valign="top">The elephant being nearly the only thing in stark focus was easy to see.  However for me, this appears to be a snapshot of a cat.  For cat lovers and owners Im sure it is cute, but for the rest of us, it is only a simple snapshot.</td>', 'The elephant being nearly the only thing in stark focus was easy to see.  However for me, this appears to be a snapshot of a cat.  For cat lovers and owners Im sure it is cute, but for the rest of us, it is only a simple snapshot.', '2010-01-03 00:06:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792424, 843180, 105441, '<td valign="top">Nice setup. Focus is a bit soft, and light is a bit hard though.</td>', 'Nice setup. Focus is a bit soft, and light is a bit hard though.', '2010-01-03 00:07:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792425, 843087, 16197, '<td valign="top">Nice image of the zebras, though there is no real pop factor for me and the letter boxing does not do anything for me.</td>', 'Nice image of the zebras, though there is no real pop factor for me and the letter boxing does not do anything for me.', '2010-01-03 00:07:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792429, 842943, 16197, '<td valign="top">This is a nice timed shot.  The depth and perspective are nice.  However for me there is too much white-space at the bottom of the image and it causes a distraction.  Also the haze over the buildings mutes out what I think could be a great colour.  I know you cannot change the haze/clouds whatever was there. Perhaps a night where the sky is a bit clearer?</td>', 'This is a nice timed shot.  The depth and perspective are nice.  However for me there is too much white-space at the bottom of the image and it causes a distraction.  Also the haze over the buildings mutes out what I think could be a great colour.  I know you cannot change the haze/clouds whatever was there. Perhaps a night where the sky is a bit clearer?', '2010-01-03 00:09:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792431, 843101, 105441, '<td valign="top">Great dog, but the leash makes it too easy, and the people and buildings clutter the background in my opinion.  Tough to blur the background on a bright day in snow.</td>', 'Great dog, but the leash makes it too easy, and the people and buildings clutter the background in my opinion.  Tough to blur the background on a bright day in snow.', '2010-01-03 00:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792432, 843320, 16197, '<td valign="top">For me there is not much here.  It appears to be two horses eating in the rain.  No real wow factor for me here.  Perhaps a stronger contrast would give a bit more life to the image.</td>', 'For me there is not much here.  It appears to be two horses eating in the rain.  No real wow factor for me here.  Perhaps a stronger contrast would give a bit more life to the image.', '2010-01-03 00:10:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792433, 840746, 16197, '<td valign="top">Very simple macro of a light.  Though being a touch yellow I feel the colour is off, if it was crystal clear or white it may have created a strong sense of spirit for me.  Though as it is, it does not hold much.</td>', 'Very simple macro of a light.  Though being a touch yellow I feel the colour is off, if it was crystal clear or white it may have created a strong sense of spirit for me.  Though as it is, it does not hold much.', '2010-01-03 00:11:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792437, 842600, 105441, '<td valign="top">Interesting effect.  Is the ball acting as a part of the lens system, allowing the background to be blurred while the same buildings are in focus in the ball?  Or is this all a post processing trick?  I like it either way.</td>', 'Interesting effect.  Is the ball acting as a part of the lens system, allowing the background to be blurred while the same buildings are in focus in the ball?  Or is this all a post processing trick?  I like it either way.', '2010-01-03 00:12:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792439, 839634, 16197, '<td valign="top">Strait on images are often lacking in wow factor.  To demonstrate this, I find the most exciting piece of the image to be the titled barrier on the curb and I wonder how it became so titled.  Was it a car, or truck that sped through? Was there a fight one night and someone was thrown against it? Was it just poorly constructed and after time its own weight started to make it tilt?  it is a neat building, though I feel there are stronger ways to show it off.</td>', 'Strait on images are often lacking in wow factor.  To demonstrate this, I find the most exciting piece of the image to be the titled barrier on the curb and I wonder how it became so titled.  Was it a car, or truck that sped through? Was there a fight one night and someone was thrown against it? Was it just poorly constructed and after time its own weight started to make it tilt?  it is a neat building, though I feel there are stronger ways to show it off.', '2010-01-03 00:13:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792441, 841548, 16197, '<td valign="top">Yes they are.  Flat in lighting, not much wow factor.  Against black may be compensating for loss of clarity, trying to get extra pop from them.  For me, they are not very exciting.  Though I am not a big flower guy myself.</td>', 'Yes they are.  Flat in lighting, not much wow factor.  Against black may be compensating for loss of clarity, trying to get extra pop from them.  For me, they are not very exciting.  Though I am not a big flower guy myself.', '2010-01-03 00:14:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792444, 842930, 105441, '<td valign="top">Ewwww.  Interesting but cluttered, perhaps the right-most portion could be cropped?</td>', 'Ewwww.  Interesting but cluttered, perhaps the right-most portion could be cropped?', '2010-01-03 00:15:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792448, 842854, 105441, '<td valign="top">Light is a bit harsh for me.</td>', 'Light is a bit harsh for me.', '2010-01-03 00:19:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792450, 841655, 105441, '<td valign="top">The sky looks like it is from another image, I will be interesting in reading the authors notes.</td>', 'The sky looks like it is from another image, I will be interesting in reading the authors notes.', '2010-01-03 00:20:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792453, 843174, 105441, '<td valign="top">Nice.  The crop on top takes away a bit, though.</td>', 'Nice.  The crop on top takes away a bit, though.', '2010-01-03 00:22:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792454, 841313, 16197, '<td valign="top">There is a nice element with the lights upon the structure on the right.  Though the sky seems or appears too bright to have so many lights in the city.  Overall it is an interesting image but for me just does not offer a strong wow factor.</td>', 'There is a nice element with the lights upon the structure on the right.  Though the sky seems or appears too bright to have so many lights in the city.  Overall it is an interesting image but for me just does not offer a strong wow factor.', '2010-01-03 00:23:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792456, 842989, 105441, '<td valign="top">I love this portrait, crazy eyes and all.</td>', 'I love this portrait, crazy eyes and all.', '2010-01-03 00:24:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792458, 839726, 105441, '<td valign="top">The hair!  Great image.</td>', 'The hair!  Great image.', '2010-01-03 00:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792461, 841434, 16197, '<td valign="top">The bane of photographer... powerlines.  I wish there was something more to this.  For me, there is no really identity or connection. I want something more and this image just does not have it.</td>', 'The bane of photographer... powerlines.  I wish there was something more to this.  For me, there is no really identity or connection. I want something more and this image just does not have it.', '2010-01-03 00:27:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792463, 843275, 16197, '<td valign="top">Interesting concept though the center framing is killin me.  Also the overly textured ground is a distraction to me.  I would have liked the sky pulled back and a richer colour in its place to give me a more sun rise/set feeling.</td>', 'Interesting concept though the center framing is killin me.  Also the overly textured ground is a distraction to me.  I would have liked the sky pulled back and a richer colour in its place to give me a more sun rise/set feeling.', '2010-01-03 00:28:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792465, 843253, 16197, '<td valign="top">Not a bad image but not a great one.  The shallow dof offers some personality though I feel it falls off too quickly because the cackles standing up would have offered a much more animalistic and raw feeling if in focus.</td>', 'Not a bad image but not a great one.  The shallow dof offers some personality though I feel it falls off too quickly because the cackles standing up would have offered a much more animalistic and raw feeling if in focus.', '2010-01-03 00:29:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792467, 842878, 16197, '<td valign="top">Cute street scene.  A nice location.  However for me there just isn''t enough push.  Maybe a bit of contrast or colour one way or the other.  But it is lacking something for me.  However it is nice.</td>', 'Cute street scene.  A nice location.  However for me there just isn''t enough push.  Maybe a bit of contrast or colour one way or the other.  But it is lacking something for me.  However it is nice.', '2010-01-03 00:30:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792479, 843022, 16197, '<td valign="top">I enjoy this piece.  The colours and twirls are fun.  It would be a great piece for painting with light challenge or extended exposure challenge.  But for a free study I feel it is not strong enough to hold up to some of the other pieces.  However it is a fantastic image.</td>', 'I enjoy this piece.  The colours and twirls are fun.  It would be a great piece for painting with light challenge or extended exposure challenge.  But for a free study I feel it is not strong enough to hold up to some of the other pieces.  However it is a fantastic image.', '2010-01-03 00:41:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792482, 842853, 16197, '<td valign="top">It is a nice image, the contrast is nice between the animal, sky and shadow.  However there seems to be a certain depth missing here.  Sure its a nice image, but just missing that wow factor.</td>', 'It is a nice image, the contrast is nice between the animal, sky and shadow.  However there seems to be a certain depth missing here.  Sure its a nice image, but just missing that wow factor.', '2010-01-03 00:42:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792484, 841653, 16197, '<td valign="top">For me the first thing I notice is that the stalks are overly smooth.  If some tool was used to smooth them I feel it went too far.  It makes a distraction for me.  If a tool wasn''t those are certainly the smoothest  talks I have seen.  Im assuming green-onions. But I am not a master chef so I have no idea exactly.  I enjoy the clarity of the container and the contrast of the strings inside.  Just the actual greenage appears faulty to me.</td>', 'For me the first thing I notice is that the stalks are overly smooth.  If some tool was used to smooth them I feel it went too far.  It makes a distraction for me.  If a tool wasn''t those are certainly the smoothest  talks I have seen.  Im assuming green-onions. But I am not a master chef so I have no idea exactly.  I enjoy the clarity of the container and the contrast of the strings inside.  Just the actual greenage appears faulty to me.', '2010-01-03 00:44:17.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5792486, 842993, 16197, '<td valign="top">For me, this piece leaves me wanting more.  The absolute cut-off of the mannequin distracts me as well as the barely visible hair.  There is no personality or dramatic appeal for me.</td>', 'For me, this piece leaves me wanting more.  The absolute cut-off of the mannequin distracts me as well as the barely visible hair.  There is no personality or dramatic appeal for me.', '2010-01-03 00:45:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792487, 838946, 16197, '<td valign="top">Not sure if it is the bulb or the technique used but it appears smoother than it should. Or maybe frosted?  Also I would have liked a bit more texture in the snow however I do enjoy the slight break between the background and snow.</td>', 'Not sure if it is the bulb or the technique used but it appears smoother than it should. Or maybe frosted?  Also I would have liked a bit more texture in the snow however I do enjoy the slight break between the background and snow.', '2010-01-03 00:46:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792489, 843234, 16197, '<td valign="top">Gotta love the little buggers.  I am happy is head is in focus.  It is a nice clean portrait of the critter.  Though for me it does not offer enough excitement or wow factor.</td>', 'Gotta love the little buggers.  I am happy is head is in focus.  It is a nice clean portrait of the critter.  Though for me it does not offer enough excitement or wow factor.', '2010-01-03 00:47:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792490, 841566, 16197, '<td valign="top">I do not speak the title language so no idea what it means.  However I do enjoy the concept behind this image.  Yet, the blown-out whites are a distraction for me.  I would have enjoyed something a bit more balanced with lights/darks.</td>', 'I do not speak the title language so no idea what it means.  However I do enjoy the concept behind this image.  Yet, the blown-out whites are a distraction for me.  I would have enjoyed something a bit more balanced with lights/darks.', '2010-01-03 00:48:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792491, 842894, 16197, '<td valign="top">I enjoy the tree on the viewers left.  However that is all I enjoy.  The street has very little light with no appeal.  The title would lead me to believe the street is the point of interest.  However for me, my eye is drawn to that single tree.</td>', 'I enjoy the tree on the viewers left.  However that is all I enjoy.  The street has very little light with no appeal.  The title would lead me to believe the street is the point of interest.  However for me, my eye is drawn to that single tree.', '2010-01-03 00:49:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792493, 843255, 16197, '<td valign="top">I can appreciate this concept and I can see how the dial is off center as if it was moving.  However I would have liked to see the motion blur with it as well as a stronger light source that creates drama.  In other words having the light to the side and possible back a little to crate shadow appeal.</td>', 'I can appreciate this concept and I can see how the dial is off center as if it was moving.  However I would have liked to see the motion blur with it as well as a stronger light source that creates drama.  In other words having the light to the side and possible back a little to crate shadow appeal.', '2010-01-03 00:51:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792505, 841140, 16197, '<td valign="top">This image has some nice elements.  However for me, it just does not offer enough wow or excitement.  Perhaps a lower camera angle would create another push or a push of colours.  Though I have to say I am happy the sun is not center frame... but its close.</td>', 'This image has some nice elements.  However for me, it just does not offer enough wow or excitement.  Perhaps a lower camera angle would create another push or a push of colours.  Though I have to say I am happy the sun is not center frame... but its close.', '2010-01-03 01:07:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792507, 842058, 16197, '<td valign="top">Nice image of the fisherman with the orange/yellow sky.  I wish that the sun was not so blown out, or perhaps even crop that area off the top of the image and only maintain a slight bit of the white/yellow and keeping most the sky a deeper orange.  As I write this it is cut off my screen above and I enjoy it more then with the added blown area.  Sometimes less is more.</td>', 'Nice image of the fisherman with the orange/yellow sky.  I wish that the sun was not so blown out, or perhaps even crop that area off the top of the image and only maintain a slight bit of the white/yellow and keeping most the sky a deeper orange.  As I write this it is cut off my screen above and I enjoy it more then with the added blown area.  Sometimes less is more.', '2010-01-03 01:09:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792525, 843235, 16197, '<td valign="top">Interesting find.  It almost has some personality but for me there is not enough dramatic appeal.</td>', 'Interesting find.  It almost has some personality but for me there is not enough dramatic appeal.', '2010-01-03 01:35:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792526, 840494, 16197, '<td valign="top">I enjoy the effects of the clouds however the rest of the image is really lacking in interest for me.</td>', 'I enjoy the effects of the clouds however the rest of the image is really lacking in interest for me.', '2010-01-03 01:36:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792528, 843318, 16197, '<td valign="top">The sky and background silhouette I really enjoy the holiday lights for me are a bore.  I suppose I would have liked something with a bit more personality and character.</td>', 'The sky and background silhouette I really enjoy the holiday lights for me are a bore.  I suppose I would have liked something with a bit more personality and character.', '2010-01-03 01:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792529, 840502, 16197, '<td valign="top">This is almost interesting though I do enjoy the large mound of snow.  It almost appears to be the macro of a flat headed nail.  The contrasts and lighting is nice as well as the delicate texture of snow many people sem ot overlook.</td>', 'This is almost interesting though I do enjoy the large mound of snow.  It almost appears to be the macro of a flat headed nail.  The contrasts and lighting is nice as well as the delicate texture of snow many people sem ot overlook.', '2010-01-03 01:38:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792607, 843229, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: It definitely lives up to its title, the sense of ''vortex'' is very well communicated. It does work as  an abstract.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: It is very harsh on the eyes - the limited number of shades and the banding make this an image than strays beyond abstract into something which is quite unphoto-like.<br/> <br/>Overall: I''m sure you''ve pulled off the look you wanted but it''s not an image I get a lot out of.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: It definitely lives up to its title, the sense of ''vortex'' is very well communicated. It does work as  an abstract. Critical stuff: It is very harsh on the eyes - the limited number of shades and the banding make this an image than strays beyond abstract into something which is quite unphoto-like. Overall: I''m sure you''ve pulled off the look you wanted but it''s not an image I get a lot out of.', '2010-01-03 03:51:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792611, 843120, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the way this is more about shape and ''flow'' than it is about the subjects themselves. The light is also effective and somewhat suggestive of care headlights - the feel you get when driving deserted roads at night. I like the coloration too - the near monochrome works very well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Somehow I wish it was a little softer to emphasise the flowing shape, a long exposure in the wind may have offered such an effect but then of course it would be a different image. I suppose I mean that the degree of sharpness you have offered here offers a little too much for the mood I get from the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: An intriguing and effective image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I like the way this is more about shape and ''flow'' than it is about the subjects themselves. The light is also effective and somewhat suggestive of care headlights - the feel you get when driving deserted roads at night. I like the coloration too - the near monochrome works very well. Critical stuff: Somehow I wish it was a little softer to emphasise the flowing shape, a long exposure in the wind may have offered such an effect but then of course it would be a different image. I suppose I mean that the degree of sharpness you have offered here offers a little too much for the mood I get from the image. Overall: An intriguing and effective image.', '2010-01-03 03:57:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792612, 838089, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: This interesting for a number of reasons, not least your aspect ratio. It does work though, it conveys a sense of the branches reaching up to the sun, try to glean as much as possible from the paltry light you have shown us. The sun itself obscured through the cloud is almost moon-like in its curtailed intensity. Most of all though, I like the detail you have captured in the lower clouds and the way that contrasts with the flatter, textureless majority of the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all really - any change would upset the balance you have created.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective and well crafted image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: This interesting for a number of reasons, not least your aspect ratio. It does work though, it conveys a sense of the branches reaching up to the sun, try to glean as much as possible from the paltry light you have shown us. The sun itself obscured through the cloud is almost moon-like in its curtailed intensity. Most of all though, I like the detail you have captured in the lower clouds and the way that contrasts with the flatter, textureless majority of the image. Critical stuff: Nothing at all really - any change would upset the balance you have created. Overall: A very effective and well crafted image.', '2010-01-03 04:02:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792614, 842600, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is very well done.</td>', 'This is very well done.', '2010-01-03 04:06:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792616, 843234, 100393, '<td valign="top">This pretty amazing really - squirrel shots are 10 a penny (done a bunch myself) but this ''pose'', this lighting and this background elevate this image to something rather special.</td>', 'This pretty amazing really - squirrel shots are 10 a penny (done a bunch myself) but this ''pose'', this lighting and this background elevate this image to something rather special.', '2010-01-03 04:08:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792624, 841225, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like the way this has an abstract feel to it - it offers something of having an overlay (but without the overlay!) Other than the plant the rest of the scene looks like it is shrink wrapped in plastic. Going back to the plant - I think it is a vital element in the image, it anchors the eye and allows it to wander out and explore. It would be a chaotic image without it. I also like the brown/blue/green colour palette.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I do wish the head / tops of eyes were a tad sharper, though I can see that this might diminish the camouflage effect.<br/> <br/>Overall: A well constructed and edited image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I really like the way this has an abstract feel to it - it offers something of having an overlay (but without the overlay!) Other than the plant the rest of the scene looks like it is shrink wrapped in plastic. Going back to the plant - I think it is a vital element in the image, it anchors the eye and allows it to wander out and explore. It would be a chaotic image without it. I also like the brown/blue/green colour palette. Critical stuff: I do wish the head / tops of eyes were a tad sharper, though I can see that this might diminish the camouflage effect. Overall: A well constructed and edited image.', '2010-01-03 04:17:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792634, 843134, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: A very interesting feel here, not sure whether this is inside or outside - reminds of a recreated street in a museum of some sort. The lighting is quite strange (in a good way), both flat and with depth at the same time. The overall subject matter confuses just as much, there is a lot of mystery in the figure, especially in relation to their position with respect to the rest of the scene.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: All of the above really, the flip side of the mystery is that the image does conspire to confound and thus frustrate a little.<br/> <br/>Overall: Made me stop, made me think.... Do I like it? I still don''t know.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: A very interesting feel here, not sure whether this is inside or outside - reminds of a recreated street in a museum of some sort. The lighting is quite strange (in a good way), both flat and with depth at the same time. The overall subject matter confuses just as much, there is a lot of mystery in the figure, especially in relation to their position with respect to the rest of the scene. Critical stuff: All of the above really, the flip side of the mystery is that the image does conspire to confound and thus frustrate a little. Overall: Made me stop, made me think.... Do I like it? I still don''t know.', '2010-01-03 04:25:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792645, 839947, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a very beautiful image - wonderful light.</td>', 'This is a very beautiful image - wonderful light.', '2010-01-03 04:44:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792648, 843201, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I really, really like this - the colour and grain, the mix of focus and blur, the inverted figures, the overall mystery of the object, the play of the light on the surface - all these elements contribute to something more than the sum of the parts.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: DPC is a better place for entries like this, images from people who understand the difference between seeing and just framing. It won''t do well, but it gets a 9 from me.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I really, really like this - the colour and grain, the mix of focus and blur, the inverted figures, the overall mystery of the object, the play of the light on the surface - all these elements contribute to something more than the sum of the parts. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: DPC is a better place for entries like this, images from people who understand the difference between seeing and just framing. It won''t do well, but it gets a 9 from me.', '2010-01-03 04:49:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792649, 842600, 103032, '<td valign="top">Creative image.  I like the focus on the sphere and the nice DOF for the background blur.  This image draws me in where I''m looking at the sphere and comparing it to the background to figure out the the buildings and shapes.  Very cool.</td>', 'Creative image.  I like the focus on the sphere and the nice DOF for the background blur.  This image draws me in where I''m looking at the sphere and comparing it to the background to figure out the the buildings and shapes.  Very cool.', '2010-01-03 04:50:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792650, 842647, 103032, '<td valign="top">Incredible symmetry, lines, and curves.  Good DOF.  I''m thinking you bumped up the saturation which I like, the colors really pop in this.  I hope this does well for you.</td>', 'Incredible symmetry, lines, and curves.  Good DOF.  I''m thinking you bumped up the saturation which I like, the colors really pop in this.  I hope this does well for you.', '2010-01-03 04:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792653, 841701, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives:This has a very dramatic feel about it, I really like the composition and the lighting is really top notch. DOF and sharpness is pretty amazing for this light level.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: In some ways the scene looks a little too contrived - I wonder if the smoke (was it a canister?), if I use my hand to mask of the left hand side of the image, with the man''s back being adjacent to the left edge it becomes (for me) a more effective image.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very, very competent work - well beyond the likes of me, but I can''t help thinking that less may have been more. Still, I do admire it. 8.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives:This has a very dramatic feel about it, I really like the composition and the lighting is really top notch. DOF and sharpness is pretty amazing for this light level. Critical stuff: In some ways the scene looks a little too contrived - I wonder if the smoke (was it a canister?), if I use my hand to mask of the left hand side of the image, with the man''s back being adjacent to the left edge it becomes (for me) a more effective image. Overall: Very, very competent work - well beyond the likes of me, but I can''t help thinking that less may have been more. Still, I do admire it. 8.', '2010-01-03 04:55:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792656, 840178, 100393, '<td valign="top">Not something you (well, me) see(s) every day. Excellent stuff.</td>', 'Not something you (well, me) see(s) every day. Excellent stuff.', '2010-01-03 04:57:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5792657, 838039, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: What an interesting scene and one that confounds the viewer - I can see the meniscus of the water adjacent to some of the branches so I assume this is lying on the surface. What I can''t work out is why the ''tree'' has such sharpness while the ripples top left are so out of focus - I''d have thought they would have been in the same focal plane. The square composition works really well - my wife just said to me that it looks like an album cover and I can see that it really does. The flower of course is the star here - a vital element that lifts your image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: There are parts of the image (the branches) that look a little over-sharpened and the highlights on the flower are perhaps a little bright - also I do find the ripples top left a little frustrating because their OOF nature, the eye is drawn there but is not satisfied.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very well composed and most interesting image - my frustration with elements of it are minor compared to the overall impact of the image. I like it.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: What an interesting scene and one that confounds the viewer - I can see the meniscus of the water adjacent to some of the branches so I assume this is lying on the surface. What I can''t work out is why the ''tree'' has such sharpness while the ripples top left are so out of focus - I''d have thought they would have been in the same focal plane. The square composition works really well - my wife just said to me that it looks like an album cover and I can see that it really does. The flower of course is the star here - a vital element that lifts your image. Critical stuff: There are parts of the image (the branches) that look a little over-sharpened and the highlights on the flower are perhaps a little bright - also I do find the ripples top left a little frustrating because their OOF nature, the eye is drawn there but is not satisfied. Overall: A very well composed and most interesting image - my frustration with elements of it are minor compared to the overall impact of the image. I like it.', '2010-01-03 04:57:30.000000', NULL, 1),
