(5798154, 842492, 109478, '<td valign="top">blue ribbon</td>', 'blue ribbon', '2010-01-06 01:41:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798220, 838621, 29904, '<td valign="top">I love that spot and all of MDO.  Nice catch with the rainbows in the waves, too bad about the wash being so overexposed.  This would have really popped with a polarizer lens and a bump up in the contrast. Good luck...</td>', 'I love that spot and all of MDO.  Nice catch with the rainbows in the waves, too bad about the wash being so overexposed.  This would have really popped with a polarizer lens and a bump up in the contrast. Good luck...', '2010-01-06 02:42:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798225, 842971, 93565, '<td valign="top">Hm, a second egret shot. Nice job keeping everything properly exposed. Your details are pretty sharp throughout. Good choice for the pose. Some of the sticks in the background distract a little, but getting a perfect background for a flying bird shot is a crapshoot.</td>', 'Hm, a second egret shot. Nice job keeping everything properly exposed. Your details are pretty sharp throughout. Good choice for the pose. Some of the sticks in the background distract a little, but getting a perfect background for a flying bird shot is a crapshoot.', '2010-01-06 02:46:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798228, 838353, 93565, '<td valign="top">I really like how the sea and the sky merge in a manner that makes it nearly impossible to separate the two. Some small bits of the boat are overexposed, but this is a minor issue. Good choice with the BW.</td>', 'I really like how the sea and the sky merge in a manner that makes it nearly impossible to separate the two. Some small bits of the boat are overexposed, but this is a minor issue. Good choice with the BW.', '2010-01-06 02:47:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798229, 843022, 93565, '<td valign="top">Cool abstract. All the different colors make me think of a party or something. Very lively feel to things. The border feels a bit overwhelming to me.</td>', 'Cool abstract. All the different colors make me think of a party or something. Very lively feel to things. The border feels a bit overwhelming to me.', '2010-01-06 02:48:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798232, 843092, 93565, '<td valign="top">Almost a menacing look to the bird''s eye, it really draws the viewer into things. Detail is excellent, as is color and saturation. The bird in the background blends into the subject a little bit, being of a similar hue, but isn''t a big deal. Good shot, and I like the pose- not the typical standing flamingo or standard headshot that is seen.</td>', 'Almost a menacing look to the bird''s eye, it really draws the viewer into things. Detail is excellent, as is color and saturation. The bird in the background blends into the subject a little bit, being of a similar hue, but isn''t a big deal. Good shot, and I like the pose- not the typical standing flamingo or standard headshot that is seen.', '2010-01-06 02:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798234, 842946, 29904, '<td valign="top">WOW!</td>', 'WOW!', '2010-01-06 02:52:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798236, 839726, 93565, '<td valign="top">Whoa, that is some bigass poofy hair. Great lighting and your composition is nice, gives the feeling that she''s poking around a corner. Her skin seems a bit unnatural though- a bit overly smooth.</td>', 'Whoa, that is some bigass poofy hair. Great lighting and your composition is nice, gives the feeling that she''s poking around a corner. Her skin seems a bit unnatural though- a bit overly smooth.', '2010-01-06 02:53:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798240, 840685, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''d suggest trying to catch him in a more active pose, and maybe try not using a centered composition for this particular subject matter. As is, the scene just feels too typical, so changing things up to try and present the duck in a new manner to the viewer will really liven things up.</td>', 'I''d suggest trying to catch him in a more active pose, and maybe try not using a centered composition for this particular subject matter. As is, the scene just feels too typical, so changing things up to try and present the duck in a new manner to the viewer will really liven things up.', '2010-01-06 02:58:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798244, 843169, 29904, '<td valign="top">This would be really awesome if it were in focus.  The line frame makes that more obvious.  Where was it taken from?</td>', 'This would be really awesome if it were in focus.  The line frame makes that more obvious.  Where was it taken from?', '2010-01-06 03:00:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798245, 842939, 93565, '<td valign="top">I like the close crop. I can''t decide what I think about the slightly off-kilter pose combined with it, though.</td>', 'I like the close crop. I can''t decide what I think about the slightly off-kilter pose combined with it, though.', '2010-01-06 03:00:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798249, 843104, 93565, '<td valign="top">Your subject matter just doesn''t do a lot to engage me. Maybe try using a very shallow depth of field in order to isolate a particular aspect so that the photo feels more unique.</td>', 'Your subject matter just doesn''t do a lot to engage me. Maybe try using a very shallow depth of field in order to isolate a particular aspect so that the photo feels more unique.', '2010-01-06 03:09:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798251, 838220, 93565, '<td valign="top">I definitely like the moodiness you''ve captured. You lost a bit of detail in the sweater, and the foliage at the bottom left bothers me a bit because of how bright it is (steals my attention), but this is a very strong photo.</td>', 'I definitely like the moodiness you''ve captured. You lost a bit of detail in the sweater, and the foliage at the bottom left bothers me a bit because of how bright it is (steals my attention), but this is a very strong photo.', '2010-01-06 03:11:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798255, 841707, 93565, '<td valign="top">Not so often that you see high fashion type shots entered here. You''ve really nailed that genre- your shot is steeped in fantasy, which is backed up by not only the pose, but the makeup and composition as well. Great shot.</td>', 'Not so often that you see high fashion type shots entered here. You''ve really nailed that genre- your shot is steeped in fantasy, which is backed up by not only the pose, but the makeup and composition as well. Great shot.', '2010-01-06 03:13:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798259, 843150, 93565, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the happy sentiments; Happy (belated) Holidays to you as well :)<br/>Consider using ambient light instead of your pop-up flash to prevent it from becoming a specular highlight on the globe, and maybe close the drapes as well.</td>', 'Thanks for the happy sentiments; Happy (belated) Holidays to you as well :)Consider using ambient light instead of your pop-up flash to prevent it from becoming a specular highlight on the globe, and maybe close the drapes as well.', '2010-01-06 03:17:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798262, 842601, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I especially like how you''ve got points of interest at every level of the photo- The background is obviously a focal point with its beautiful color and streaming sun rays, but the trees frame things nicely and the people all staring off into the sunset are neat too. I like that you have kept them from becoming silhouettes, as well.</td>', 'Great shot. I especially like how you''ve got points of interest at every level of the photo- The background is obviously a focal point with its beautiful color and streaming sun rays, but the trees frame things nicely and the people all staring off into the sunset are neat too. I like that you have kept them from becoming silhouettes, as well.', '2010-01-06 03:18:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798271, 843230, 93565, '<td valign="top">Cute pose with the leg stretched way up high like that. I think I would''ve preferred the shot stopped down a bit so that all the moss was focused.</td>', 'Cute pose with the leg stretched way up high like that. I think I would''ve preferred the shot stopped down a bit so that all the moss was focused.', '2010-01-06 03:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798274, 839634, 93565, '<td valign="top">This one is so close to being centered that I would''ve just completely centered it, especially since you''ve got very good symmetry going on. Sky is a bit drab, but then, controlling the weather isn''t exactly a simple premise.</td>', 'This one is so close to being centered that I would''ve just completely centered it, especially since you''ve got very good symmetry going on. Sky is a bit drab, but then, controlling the weather isn''t exactly a simple premise.', '2010-01-06 03:30:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798276, 842846, 93565, '<td valign="top">Very cool area to photograph, and I''m curious to see where this was taken after the challenge. Maybe bring up the brightness in the rock in the bottom right and the forest top left, but that''s it. The colors on this are really nice.</td>', 'Very cool area to photograph, and I''m curious to see where this was taken after the challenge. Maybe bring up the brightness in the rock in the bottom right and the forest top left, but that''s it. The colors on this are really nice.', '2010-01-06 03:32:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798278, 843176, 93565, '<td valign="top">This totally made me think of American Spirit as soon as I saw it. I like the harsh side lighting on the chief, and how everything else has been underexposed. Nice subject isolation.</td>', 'This totally made me think of American Spirit as soon as I saw it. I like the harsh side lighting on the chief, and how everything else has been underexposed. Nice subject isolation.', '2010-01-06 03:33:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798280, 842207, 93565, '<td valign="top">Things are a bit busy and cluttered, so it''s a bit hard to see what should be focused upon.</td>', 'Things are a bit busy and cluttered, so it''s a bit hard to see what should be focused upon.', '2010-01-06 03:35:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798282, 838985, 52765, '<td valign="top">8 for the comedy aspect</td>', '8 for the comedy aspect', '2010-01-06 03:36:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798283, 842950, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice "glowing" feeling to this, but there seems to be little direction given to things.</td>', 'Nice "glowing" feeling to this, but there seems to be little direction given to things.', '2010-01-06 03:37:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798285, 840793, 93565, '<td valign="top">Good find with the icicle. Maybe crop out the top left bit, and think about a lower ISO- there''s some grain here (or, alternatively, convert to BW and accentuate it, which would work well with the whole "Cold Afternoon" thing).</td>', 'Good find with the icicle. Maybe crop out the top left bit, and think about a lower ISO- there''s some grain here (or, alternatively, convert to BW and accentuate it, which would work well with the whole "Cold Afternoon" thing).', '2010-01-06 03:39:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798289, 843137, 93565, '<td valign="top">I like the smug expression. Great light that softly wraps around, too.</td>', 'I like the smug expression. Great light that softly wraps around, too.', '2010-01-06 03:42:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798295, 842589, 93565, '<td valign="top">Seems like a sorta strange place for a duck to go sit, but I like it. Much more interesting than a duck just sitting upon the water.</td>', 'Seems like a sorta strange place for a duck to go sit, but I like it. Much more interesting than a duck just sitting upon the water.', '2010-01-06 03:46:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798297, 838946, 93565, '<td valign="top">Very simple and well done photo. I could easily see this selling well as a stock photo, as it conveys the holidays very effectively.</td>', 'Very simple and well done photo. I could easily see this selling well as a stock photo, as it conveys the holidays very effectively.', '2010-01-06 03:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798299, 840929, 93565, '<td valign="top">Cool bit of architecture you''ve stumbled upon- good abstract architecture shot. It reminds me of another photo I''ve seen on DPC before... but I can''t find it at the moment. The sky works very well with the tones of the building.</td>', 'Cool bit of architecture you''ve stumbled upon- good abstract architecture shot. It reminds me of another photo I''ve seen on DPC before... but I can''t find it at the moment. The sky works very well with the tones of the building.', '2010-01-06 03:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798301, 842212, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great silhouette, and the fog really adds to this. Your choice of a border, though thick, fits the scene well in my eyes.</td>', 'Great silhouette, and the fog really adds to this. Your choice of a border, though thick, fits the scene well in my eyes.', '2010-01-06 03:51:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798302, 842918, 93565, '<td valign="top">She is a bit underexposed, and lacking in contrast a bit, as well. I''m not too sure about using a black hat with a black background- the two merge together and look strange.</td>', 'She is a bit underexposed, and lacking in contrast a bit, as well. I''m not too sure about using a black hat with a black background- the two merge together and look strange.', '2010-01-06 03:52:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798368, 843297, 93565, '<td valign="top">Cool shot of the castle. The individually gleaming lights are really quite a sight to behold. The tree at bottom right obscures things a bit though.</td>', 'Cool shot of the castle. The individually gleaming lights are really quite a sight to behold. The tree at bottom right obscures things a bit though.', '2010-01-06 04:47:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798370, 843253, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great shot of a coyote. It can definitely be hard to approach these guys, so good job. Nice choice of aperture too, really brings the viewer''s attention to where it belongs- the animal''s face.</td>', 'Great shot of a coyote. It can definitely be hard to approach these guys, so good job. Nice choice of aperture too, really brings the viewer''s attention to where it belongs- the animal''s face.', '2010-01-06 04:48:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798371, 842995, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice cloud formations you''ve found, and the sunset itself isn''t too bad either :) I enjoy how the jet contrail goes literally "off into the sunset," as well.</td>', 'Nice cloud formations you''ve found, and the sunset itself isn''t too bad either :) I enjoy how the jet contrail goes literally "off into the sunset," as well.', '2010-01-06 04:48:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798397, 843088, 93565, '<td valign="top">Good Christmas lights photo. Gives a nice warm feeling to things. Not too sure what is causing it but there is some strange blurring/whiteness just to the left of the roof''s peak.</td>', 'Good Christmas lights photo. Gives a nice warm feeling to things. Not too sure what is causing it but there is some strange blurring/whiteness just to the left of the roof''s peak.', '2010-01-06 05:10:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798400, 843051, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great BW image. There''s a whole lot of cool textures going on here to be looked at in greater detail. Lots of leading lines all pulling the viewer through the train station. I also really enjoy the contrast between the moving train and the seemingly static pedestrians.</td>', 'Great BW image. There''s a whole lot of cool textures going on here to be looked at in greater detail. Lots of leading lines all pulling the viewer through the train station. I also really enjoy the contrast between the moving train and the seemingly static pedestrians.', '2010-01-06 05:12:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798401, 840298, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice application of a ringlight- your lighting is quite soft and well diffused. I don''t quite follow the purple paint though.</td>', 'Nice application of a ringlight- your lighting is quite soft and well diffused. I don''t quite follow the purple paint though.', '2010-01-06 05:14:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798403, 842970, 93565, '<td valign="top">Classic expression. Kid''s can make the craziest faces. The lighting on his face helps exaggerate the face. I wonder if a slightly slower shutter would have still kept the face sharp but added some more nice blur to the arm?</td>', 'Classic expression. Kid''s can make the craziest faces. The lighting on his face helps exaggerate the face. I wonder if a slightly slower shutter would have still kept the face sharp but added some more nice blur to the arm?', '2010-01-06 05:16:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798405, 842203, 93565, '<td valign="top">The fisheye really helps to magnify the vastness of the building, and the placement of people has a nice feel of balance to it. Nice "street" shot.</td>', 'The fisheye really helps to magnify the vastness of the building, and the placement of people has a nice feel of balance to it. Nice "street" shot.', '2010-01-06 05:18:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798408, 842944, 93565, '<td valign="top">Perhaps I''m being obtuse, but I really don''t understand your title. I like the idea of the belt and creating interest through DoF. I also like the marble in the blurred region, but am not so much a fan of the one that is focused. Not really sure why I feel that way though.</td>', 'Perhaps I''m being obtuse, but I really don''t understand your title. I like the idea of the belt and creating interest through DoF. I also like the marble in the blurred region, but am not so much a fan of the one that is focused. Not really sure why I feel that way though.', '2010-01-06 05:22:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798411, 843234, 93565, '<td valign="top">Probably one of the better squirrel photos I''ve ever seen.The texture and color of the fur is very good. Though the pose is somewhat typical of squirrels, I like it quite a bit here. I''d like to see a bit more DoF to get the details out of that giant bushy tail, but I like it as it is.</td>', 'Probably one of the better squirrel photos I''ve ever seen.The texture and color of the fur is very good. Though the pose is somewhat typical of squirrels, I like it quite a bit here. I''d like to see a bit more DoF to get the details out of that giant bushy tail, but I like it as it is.', '2010-01-06 05:24:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798415, 843283, 93565, '<td valign="top">Interesting forest you''ve found. The gnarled trees are pretty foreboding. Looks like you might have had some water drops on your lens during the capture? It''d be nice to see those go. You can decrease the "obviousness" of them by using dodge in PS.</td>', 'Interesting forest you''ve found. The gnarled trees are pretty foreboding. Looks like you might have had some water drops on your lens during the capture? It''d be nice to see those go. You can decrease the "obviousness" of them by using dodge in PS.', '2010-01-06 05:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798419, 842952, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''m not too sure if I''m correct about this, but the image as a whole feels like it''s been contorted. It seems as though the width was decreased without the proper decrease in height to match, squishing everything in. I''d also prefer the DoF to be centered on the horses themselves, not behind, since they are the subjects.</td>', 'I''m not too sure if I''m correct about this, but the image as a whole feels like it''s been contorted. It seems as though the width was decreased without the proper decrease in height to match, squishing everything in. I''d also prefer the DoF to be centered on the horses themselves, not behind, since they are the subjects.', '2010-01-06 05:29:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798421, 841599, 93565, '<td valign="top">Good cardinal shot. Details could be a little sharper but are pretty good to begin with. I like the bits of snow that you''ve included.</td>', 'Good cardinal shot. Details could be a little sharper but are pretty good to begin with. I like the bits of snow that you''ve included.', '2010-01-06 05:33:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798422, 843010, 93565, '<td valign="top">Admittedly, you''ve done a great job of spicing things up here, but the subject matter just doesn''t engage me much at all.</td>', 'Admittedly, you''ve done a great job of spicing things up here, but the subject matter just doesn''t engage me much at all.', '2010-01-06 05:34:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798423, 841671, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great hoarfrost picture. I''m not sure I''ve ever seen it quite so spikey. The only thing I could recommend is maybe getting more up close and personal with it, but this is still an interesting shot.</td>', 'Great hoarfrost picture. I''m not sure I''ve ever seen it quite so spikey. The only thing I could recommend is maybe getting more up close and personal with it, but this is still an interesting shot.', '2010-01-06 05:35:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798424, 843257, 93565, '<td valign="top">Very cool warping of the image in the windows. The color changes are very interesting as well. For some reason, it feels as though the image is crooked, although I know that isn''t the case (yes I checked).</td>', 'Very cool warping of the image in the windows. The color changes are very interesting as well. For some reason, it feels as though the image is crooked, although I know that isn''t the case (yes I checked).', '2010-01-06 05:36:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798425, 843235, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice colors on the buildings. I think the owners are a little confused... I don''t think puffins are tropical...</td>', 'Nice colors on the buildings. I think the owners are a little confused... I don''t think puffins are tropical...', '2010-01-06 05:44:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798427, 843013, 93565, '<td valign="top">I really enjoy the BW treatment you''ve given this. Would maybe like to see the blown white area on the right removed from the shot by rotating the PoV but I like this as is too.</td>', 'I really enjoy the BW treatment you''ve given this. Would maybe like to see the blown white area on the right removed from the shot by rotating the PoV but I like this as is too.', '2010-01-06 05:46:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798428, 838554, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''m assuming the tinge of color is from either morning or evening lighting, but it makes things appear almost pink and strange.</td>', 'I''m assuming the tinge of color is from either morning or evening lighting, but it makes things appear almost pink and strange.', '2010-01-06 05:48:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798429, 842930, 93565, '<td valign="top">I enjoy how you managed to keep the poses for your two subjects somewhat similar, it provides for a strange juxtaposition. A couple of small areas of highlights are blown, but they aren''t terribly distracting. Might be a bit macabre for the DPC crowd as a whole, but I find it to be an interesting shot.</td>', 'I enjoy how you managed to keep the poses for your two subjects somewhat similar, it provides for a strange juxtaposition. A couple of small areas of highlights are blown, but they aren''t terribly distracting. Might be a bit macabre for the DPC crowd as a whole, but I find it to be an interesting shot.', '2010-01-06 05:48:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798432, 839423, 93565, '<td valign="top">Quality cityscape- a couple of the lights are a bit bright but everything else is very pleasing. The reflections are a subtle addition to the scene, and rounds out the foreground well.</td>', 'Quality cityscape- a couple of the lights are a bit bright but everything else is very pleasing. The reflections are a subtle addition to the scene, and rounds out the foreground well.', '2010-01-06 05:50:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798434, 839732, 93565, '<td valign="top">Another cool cityscape, and an excellent use of fisheye. The distortion really makes the picture here.</td>', 'Another cool cityscape, and an excellent use of fisheye. The distortion really makes the picture here.', '2010-01-06 05:51:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798435, 843270, 93565, '<td valign="top">Excellent change-up from the normal infant portrait. Perfect pose and I quite like the lighting.</td>', 'Excellent change-up from the normal infant portrait. Perfect pose and I quite like the lighting.', '2010-01-06 05:52:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798437, 843083, 93565, '<td valign="top">Good focus and detail. The background works very well with the subject matter''s coloration.</td>', 'Good focus and detail. The background works very well with the subject matter''s coloration.', '2010-01-06 05:58:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798438, 839137, 93565, '<td valign="top">I like the idea behind the shot. The daylight seems a bit harsh and things are a bit washed out, so maybe try to shoot earlier in the day when the sunlight isn''t quite so intense.</td>', 'I like the idea behind the shot. The daylight seems a bit harsh and things are a bit washed out, so maybe try to shoot earlier in the day when the sunlight isn''t quite so intense.', '2010-01-06 05:59:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798443, 842853, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice job making use of something that would normally prove to be a hindrance. The grid line also reminds me of grill marks, so there is a bit of a double entendre there.</td>', 'Nice job making use of something that would normally prove to be a hindrance. The grid line also reminds me of grill marks, so there is a bit of a double entendre there.', '2010-01-06 06:02:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798444, 843303, 93565, '<td valign="top">I can''t help but think the lake in the foreground is stealing all the attention from the volcano in the background.</td>', 'I can''t help but think the lake in the foreground is stealing all the attention from the volcano in the background.', '2010-01-06 06:03:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798447, 840048, 93565, '<td valign="top">I like the colors and cloud texture, but I think you''ve gone a bit far with the Topaz here.</td>', 'I like the colors and cloud texture, but I think you''ve gone a bit far with the Topaz here.', '2010-01-06 06:07:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798449, 843295, 93565, '<td valign="top">Not a bad running dog shot, but higher speed running than this is typically where you get the best results. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=676366" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/859/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_676366.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/859/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_676366.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/859/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_676366.jpg"/></a> Like that one. There''s another one somewhere on the site too that illustrates what I''m talking about but I can''t find it. The other one is a head-on shot like yours, in BW.</td>', 'Not a bad running dog shot, but higher speed running than this is typically where you get the best results.  Like that one. There''s another one somewhere on the site too that illustrates what I''m talking about but I can''t find it. The other one is a head-on shot like yours, in BW.', '2010-01-06 06:10:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798451, 843314, 93565, '<td valign="top">Good alternative to the standard sunrise picture. I like the inclusion of the forest and the low level clouds/fog in the background are interesting as well.</td>', 'Good alternative to the standard sunrise picture. I like the inclusion of the forest and the low level clouds/fog in the background are interesting as well.', '2010-01-06 06:12:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798452, 840238, 93565, '<td valign="top">Nice control of DoF on her face, and you''ve done a nice job with the lighting too.</td>', 'Nice control of DoF on her face, and you''ve done a nice job with the lighting too.', '2010-01-06 06:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798453, 841324, 93565, '<td valign="top">The desaturation you''ve employed really makes the colors pop, making an ordinary fly into an intriguing subject.</td>', 'The desaturation you''ve employed really makes the colors pop, making an ordinary fly into an intriguing subject.', '2010-01-06 06:18:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798455, 842854, 93565, '<td valign="top">Because of how dark her attire is, a white background might be more appropriate to help separate her from it. Her expression looks slightly uneasy and awkward.</td>', 'Because of how dark her attire is, a white background might be more appropriate to help separate her from it. Her expression looks slightly uneasy and awkward.', '2010-01-06 06:20:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798458, 840800, 93565, '<td valign="top">That building hiding in the depths of the shot, and especially the trees reaching out to frame it, combine to make this a great shot.</td>', 'That building hiding in the depths of the shot, and especially the trees reaching out to frame it, combine to make this a great shot.', '2010-01-06 06:24:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798460, 842965, 93565, '<td valign="top">This is another example of using shadows effectively to convey a message (another entry in this month''s FS did the same thing). I also like that you have added an additional meaning to an existing work of art.</td>', 'This is another example of using shadows effectively to convey a message (another entry in this month''s FS did the same thing). I also like that you have added an additional meaning to an existing work of art.', '2010-01-06 06:26:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798463, 841432, 93565, '<td valign="top">The snowflakes captured in this shot are very good- no terribly close flakes that produce a huge blur and become distracting, yet the flakes are still very visible. You integrated them into the theme of your photo very well.</td>', 'The snowflakes captured in this shot are very good- no terribly close flakes that produce a huge blur and become distracting, yet the flakes are still very visible. You integrated them into the theme of your photo very well.', '2010-01-06 06:29:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798469, 841679, 93565, '<td valign="top">The cat on the left certainly looks as though they are literally bathing in the sunlight. In addition to the cat''s poses, the shadow is rather interesting, especially with the window framing.</td>', 'The cat on the left certainly looks as though they are literally bathing in the sunlight. In addition to the cat''s poses, the shadow is rather interesting, especially with the window framing.', '2010-01-06 06:34:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798532, 843252, 18655, '<td valign="top">Beautiful scene and very well done. Good choice with the rocks in the foreground!</td>', 'Beautiful scene and very well done. Good choice with the rocks in the foreground!', '2010-01-06 07:14:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798535, 840393, 18655, '<td valign="top">Nicely done and colorful. Good perspective</td>', 'Nicely done and colorful. Good perspective', '2010-01-06 07:18:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798542, 842973, 93565, '<td valign="top">Good candidate for BW. Maybe a little bit more grunge processing to match the character of the boat, but good entry.</td>', 'Good candidate for BW. Maybe a little bit more grunge processing to match the character of the boat, but good entry.', '2010-01-06 07:27:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798546, 843317, 93565, '<td valign="top">That''s a pretty cool root structure. It really looks as though they are tentacles, reaching out and gripping the wall. I''m curious to see what the rest of the tree and wall look like, as the wall has interesting textures and colors (a picture of the wall on its own would also make a nice overlay).</td>', 'That''s a pretty cool root structure. It really looks as though they are tentacles, reaching out and gripping the wall. I''m curious to see what the rest of the tree and wall look like, as the wall has interesting textures and colors (a picture of the wall on its own would also make a nice overlay).', '2010-01-06 07:29:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798549, 843309, 93565, '<td valign="top">A well done, quirky family portrait. Two minor issues- the youngest arm is cut off and you can just barely see the wrinkles in the background. Otherwise, excellent through and through.</td>', 'A well done, quirky family portrait. Two minor issues- the youngest arm is cut off and you can just barely see the wrinkles in the background. Otherwise, excellent through and through.', '2010-01-06 07:30:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798559, 842647, 93565, '<td valign="top">There a few architectural photos in this FS that are not only captured very well, but that also depict interesting areas. Yours definitely fits in that category. Good job using the lines of the building to pull the viewer through the scene.</td>', 'There a few architectural photos in this FS that are not only captured very well, but that also depict interesting areas. Yours definitely fits in that category. Good job using the lines of the building to pull the viewer through the scene.', '2010-01-06 07:34:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798562, 843120, 93565, '<td valign="top">The wavy branches have a definite spooky or fairy-tale feel to them. I don''t know if you accomplished this by heavy burning or selective lighting, but the end result is pretty cool.</td>', 'The wavy branches have a definite spooky or fairy-tale feel to them. I don''t know if you accomplished this by heavy burning or selective lighting, but the end result is pretty cool.', '2010-01-06 07:36:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798563, 843316, 93565, '<td valign="top">I feel like the best part of this image (the details) has somewhat been obliterated. It seems the details are especially important due to your title, so I don''t quite understand the approach taken. Great location for shots.</td>', 'I feel like the best part of this image (the details) has somewhat been obliterated. It seems the details are especially important due to your title, so I don''t quite understand the approach taken. Great location for shots.', '2010-01-06 07:36:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798566, 842922, 93565, '<td valign="top">The overuse of Topaz has led to some noticeable noise issues in the sky. In the future, to avoid this, selectively apply your filter by masking off the sky. Alternately, you can apply noise reduction to the sky prior to applying Topaz and that should help things out as well.</td>', 'The overuse of Topaz has led to some noticeable noise issues in the sky. In the future, to avoid this, selectively apply your filter by masking off the sky. Alternately, you can apply noise reduction to the sky prior to applying Topaz and that should help things out as well.', '2010-01-06 07:38:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798577, 843108, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great job composing the shot; I''m especially fond of the pathway angling to the right and then back across the frame in the opposite direction.</td>', 'Great job composing the shot; I''m especially fond of the pathway angling to the right and then back across the frame in the opposite direction.', '2010-01-06 07:42:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798586, 841793, 93565, '<td valign="top">This portrait has a good deal going for it. Nice posing, light, and background. I like the addition of snow, but wish there wasn''t the one snowflake falling between the camera and her hat. It also looks like stopping down a little would have helped a bit, since her right eye has lost a bit of sharpness.</td>', 'This portrait has a good deal going for it. Nice posing, light, and background. I like the addition of snow, but wish there wasn''t the one snowflake falling between the camera and her hat. It also looks like stopping down a little would have helped a bit, since her right eye has lost a bit of sharpness.', '2010-01-06 07:47:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798590, 838577, 93565, '<td valign="top">For whatever reason, when I look at your photo I don''t associate it with your choice for title. Having said that, I think this is an excellent candid.</td>', 'For whatever reason, when I look at your photo I don''t associate it with your choice for title. Having said that, I think this is an excellent candid.', '2010-01-06 07:49:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798593, 842704, 93565, '<td valign="top">Not sure what to attribute it to, but there''s a strange glowing about your photo that doesn''t quite appeal to me.</td>', 'Not sure what to attribute it to, but there''s a strange glowing about your photo that doesn''t quite appeal to me.', '2010-01-06 07:50:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798601, 843107, 62357, '<td valign="top">Not even after a sauna? What a wonderful winter wonderland!</td>', 'Not even after a sauna? What a wonderful winter wonderland!', '2010-01-06 08:01:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798662, 842193, 105130, '<td valign="top">Great focus, nice moment, like the flare and the post-processing. I would have got rid of that thing in the top left though.</td>', 'Great focus, nice moment, like the flare and the post-processing. I would have got rid of that thing in the top left though.', '2010-01-06 08:46:56.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5798718, 842922, 105130, '<td valign="top">It looks like you opened up Photomatix and moved all the sliders to the far right. Sadly, you ruined a photo that actually had potential.</td>', 'It looks like you opened up Photomatix and moved all the sliders to the far right. Sadly, you ruined a photo that actually had potential.', '2010-01-06 09:23:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798721, 842928, 105130, '<td valign="top">Lovely and crisp. Would love to see it slightly bigger.</td>', 'Lovely and crisp. Would love to see it slightly bigger.', '2010-01-06 09:28:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798845, 841567, 100789, '<td valign="top">This photo caught my attention right away. Bittersweet and tender, nicely done!</td>', 'This photo caught my attention right away. Bittersweet and tender, nicely done!', '2010-01-06 10:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798848, 841447, 100789, '<td valign="top">Wow... very nice!</td>', 'Wow... very nice!', '2010-01-06 10:31:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798853, 843228, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: A nice study in grungy pipework and the coloration is well suited to the subject matter. I like that you haven''t lost the sense of depth amongst the ''clutter''.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The amount of intrinsic interest in the scene is fairly low - many voters will skip by at a rate of knots.<br/> <br/>Overall: A nice rendition of this scene but one that might not hold the viewers interest for them to explore the scene fully.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: A nice study in grungy pipework and the coloration is well suited to the subject matter. I like that you haven''t lost the sense of depth amongst the ''clutter''. Critical stuff: The amount of intrinsic interest in the scene is fairly low - many voters will skip by at a rate of knots. Overall: A nice rendition of this scene but one that might not hold the viewers interest for them to explore the scene fully.', '2010-01-06 10:33:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798857, 843235, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: An interesting scene - you have captured the bizarre juxtaposition of the themed cafe with the chilly waters and landscape beyond. Technically is is very well done - great light and coloration.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not too much really - I think you have gotten full value out of this scene.<br/> <br/>Overall: A well executed rendition of a curious scene.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: An interesting scene - you have captured the bizarre juxtaposition of the themed cafe with the chilly waters and landscape beyond. Technically is is very well done - great light and coloration. Critical stuff: Not too much really - I think you have gotten full value out of this scene. Overall: A well executed rendition of a curious scene.', '2010-01-06 10:37:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798858, 843254, 105130, '<td valign="top">I''d love to see this as a high-contrast B&amp;W. Great photo nonetheless.</td>', 'I''d love to see this as a high-contrast B&W. Great photo nonetheless.', '2010-01-06 10:38:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798869, 842925, 105130, '<td valign="top">Love it. Got one of my top votes. Good luck!</td>', 'Love it. Got one of my top votes. Good luck!', '2010-01-06 10:48:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798877, 842925, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Such a dynamic image - I think you must have moved the camera vertically on a tripod in the snow. It works tremendously well. The monochrome, high contrast treatment is perfect for the subject matter.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image - a brilliant fusion of subject, technique and edit.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Such a dynamic image - I think you must have moved the camera vertically on a tripod in the snow. It works tremendously well. The monochrome, high contrast treatment is perfect for the subject matter. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: A very effective image - a brilliant fusion of subject, technique and edit.', '2010-01-06 10:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798891, 843348, 105130, '<td valign="top">Looks like he <i>ju-ust</i> made it out of a sizeable close out. Nice moment you''ve captured here, not sure how many non-surfers will appreciate it though.</td>', 'Looks like he ju-ust made it out of a sizeable close out. Nice moment you''ve captured here, not sure how many non-surfers will appreciate it though.', '2010-01-06 11:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798894, 843173, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Oh, I really like this - but what''s really annoying me is that I don''t know why! What sort of a critique is this going to be?? Let me try - I like how it is inside / out / outside / in; hidden and revealed; public and private; free and constrained. Does any of that make sense?<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Perhaps the crop? I keep wishing the window was central in the frame but I suspect if I played around with it, it would look better just as it is.<br/> <br/>Overall: So much more than the sum of its parts - taken by someone who really ''sees''.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Oh, I really like this - but what''s really annoying me is that I don''t know why! What sort of a critique is this going to be?? Let me try - I like how it is inside / out / outside / in; hidden and revealed; public and private; free and constrained. Does any of that make sense? Critical stuff: Perhaps the crop? I keep wishing the window was central in the frame but I suspect if I played around with it, it would look better just as it is. Overall: So much more than the sum of its parts - taken by someone who really ''sees''.', '2010-01-06 11:05:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798899, 843137, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Very unconventional portrait and so very, very well executed - well lit, well shot, well processed.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I hate looking at the image; I''m the most anti-smoking person I know and I''ve seriously struggled to look at the image for as long it has taken to write the comment (I know that must seem strange to a smoker).<br/> <br/>Overall: Very good work albeit one I really, really don''t enjoy.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Very unconventional portrait and so very, very well executed - well lit, well shot, well processed. Critical stuff: I hate looking at the image; I''m the most anti-smoking person I know and I''ve seriously struggled to look at the image for as long it has taken to write the comment (I know that must seem strange to a smoker). Overall: Very good work albeit one I really, really don''t enjoy.', '2010-01-06 11:09:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798904, 843257, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Nicely framed frames! Excellent coloration and I like the distortions too. I think your choice of aspect ratio works very well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Those not attracted by studies of geometry might not have too much time for this.<br/> <br/>Overall: A well balanced image, the shooting and editing match the subject matter very well indeed.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Nicely framed frames! Excellent coloration and I like the distortions too. I think your choice of aspect ratio works very well. Critical stuff: Those not attracted by studies of geometry might not have too much time for this. Overall: A well balanced image, the shooting and editing match the subject matter very well indeed.', '2010-01-06 11:12:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798907, 843101, 100393, '<td valign="top">I love the POV on this image. Great looking dog too!</td>', 'I love the POV on this image. Great looking dog too!', '2010-01-06 11:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798911, 842930, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: An interesting choice of subject - a brave entry. I think the general balance of the image is just about right - albeit with the caveats below.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the slightly angled composition distracts from your subject somewhat. Also, although the pink pig is powerful, I think a monochrome presentation of this work may have been better received.<br/> <br/>Overall: A good capture of a good slice of life (and ham!).</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: An interesting choice of subject - a brave entry. I think the general balance of the image is just about right - albeit with the caveats below. Critical stuff: I think the slightly angled composition distracts from your subject somewhat. Also, although the pink pig is powerful, I think a monochrome presentation of this work may have been better received. Overall: A good capture of a good slice of life (and ham!).', '2010-01-06 11:17:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798915, 842985, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the honesty of this shot and the effort you have gone to in preserving a frontal facade - we feel like we are just sliding past in a car (just like most people do I bet).<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I don''t know if you have Photoshop but the lens correction tool would have allowed you to compensate for the perspective a little and bring it that final tad square.<br/> <br/>Overall: Not the most naturally engaging of shots but one which makes us reflect on the world we pass by every day.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I like the honesty of this shot and the effort you have gone to in preserving a frontal facade - we feel like we are just sliding past in a car (just like most people do I bet). Critical stuff: I don''t know if you have Photoshop but the lens correction tool would have allowed you to compensate for the perspective a little and bring it that final tad square. Overall: Not the most naturally engaging of shots but one which makes us reflect on the world we pass by every day.', '2010-01-06 11:20:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798920, 842838, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Brave, brave, brave! I love it! It''s like you''ve painted with noise, quite masterful.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Bold, refreshing and great. 10.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Brave, brave, brave! I love it! It''s like you''ve painted with noise, quite masterful. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Bold, refreshing and great. 10.', '2010-01-06 11:24:06.000000', NULL, 1),
