(5798957, 837979, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Interesting high macro offered with an almost clinical presentation. Quite different to most ladybug shots we see.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not a fan of the reflection / highlight - was your light source diffused at all?<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting shot albeit a little bit ugly!</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Interesting high macro offered with an almost clinical presentation. Quite different to most ladybug shots we see. Critical stuff: I''m not a fan of the reflection / highlight - was your light source diffused at all? Overall: An interesting shot albeit a little bit ugly!', '2010-01-06 11:40:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798966, 841754, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the ''feel'' of this image and how it makes me stop and look. I really like the grainy, scratchy look too. I also like the vignette.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not too much of a fan of the blur - at first I thought it was a Lensbaby shot but I''ve never got a shot where focus drifts and then returns as it does here.<br/> <br/>Overall: An intriguing shot but that I find a little unsatisfying.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I like the ''feel'' of this image and how it makes me stop and look. I really like the grainy, scratchy look too. I also like the vignette. Critical stuff: I''m not too much of a fan of the blur - at first I thought it was a Lensbaby shot but I''ve never got a shot where focus drifts and then returns as it does here. Overall: An intriguing shot but that I find a little unsatisfying.', '2010-01-06 11:44:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798974, 838639, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: I think you have to offer something pretty close to your vision here, it does seem to be well executed. You have managed to make me most curious about the landscape beyond - it actually looks like a poppy field!<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m afraid I''m not a fan of this image - I find it to be a little drab, everything seems to be choked back in an effort to resist any possibility that the image might delight.<br/> <br/>Overall: A strange one to be sure, I can see what you''ve gone for - it''s just not an image I''m responding well to.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: I think you have to offer something pretty close to your vision here, it does seem to be well executed. You have managed to make me most curious about the landscape beyond - it actually looks like a poppy field! Critical stuff: I''m afraid I''m not a fan of this image - I find it to be a little drab, everything seems to be choked back in an effort to resist any possibility that the image might delight. Overall: A strange one to be sure, I can see what you''ve gone for - it''s just not an image I''m responding well to.', '2010-01-06 11:49:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798977, 843274, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Great perspective and coloration here and the blurred presentation allow us to see form over structure.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not sure what you could''ve done to avoid it but I don''t like the blow highlights, they lead the eye away from the blue trails.<br/> <br/>Overall: An effective image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Great perspective and coloration here and the blurred presentation allow us to see form over structure. Critical stuff: I''m not sure what you could''ve done to avoid it but I don''t like the blow highlights, they lead the eye away from the blue trails. Overall: An effective image.', '2010-01-06 11:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798984, 840538, 100393, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award: <br/> <br/>Positives: Very nice shot - well caught and well presented, I like her striped sleeve - it helps to draw the eye straight to her and keep it there.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m a bit less convinced by the tones , it looks a little like information has been lost somewhere.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective image.</td>', 'OK, I''m going through the Free Study submissions, purposefully finding those images I think are shot with a less conventional eye - this is one of those images! Thanks for offering something that isn''t just DPC friendly eye-candy (though of course there''s nothing wrong with eye-candy). I''ll be picking one of these images for the Mu (most underrated) award:  Positives: Very nice shot - well caught and well presented, I like her striped sleeve - it helps to draw the eye straight to her and keep it there. Critical stuff: I''m a bit less convinced by the tones , it looks a little like information has been lost somewhere. Overall: A very effective image.', '2010-01-06 11:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5798988, 841561, 75585, '<td valign="top">I REALLY like this and gave it an 8 - but wanted to come back and comment.  I wish the kitty was looking at us too and your bg blowout light is a bit hot on his left (right as we are looking at it) shoulder which causes it to fade in intensity on the BG to the far left of the image.  But I know this because I have the same problem - I need to get a long slim softbox 10x36 or so on a boom to get more even light on my white BG.  Is that a ragdoll?  Reminds me of my little Scooter when he was a babe :-)  By the way, love his freckles!!</td>', 'I REALLY like this and gave it an 8 - but wanted to come back and comment.  I wish the kitty was looking at us too and your bg blowout light is a bit hot on his left (right as we are looking at it) shoulder which causes it to fade in intensity on the BG to the far left of the image.  But I know this because I have the same problem - I need to get a long slim softbox 10x36 or so on a boom to get more even light on my white BG.  Is that a ragdoll?  Reminds me of my little Scooter when he was a babe :-)  By the way, love his freckles!!', '2010-01-06 11:56:05.000000', NULL, 1),
