(5802343, 842995, 67152, '<td valign="top">Delightful Robert.  The contrail makes the shot, providing a wonderful balance of light in the upper left to the houses in the lower right.</td>', 'Delightful Robert.  The contrail makes the shot, providing a wonderful balance of light in the upper left to the houses in the lower right.', '2010-01-08 10:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5802347, 841748, 38032, '<td valign="top">Really interesting processing on this.  Look almost hand-drawn or vector illustrated in some of the details.<br/> <br/>I think you successfully anthropomorphised a lion unlike I have seen - the "expression" appears pensive and human.<br/> <br/>Nice to look at for sure!  Congrats.</td>', 'Really interesting processing on this.  Look almost hand-drawn or vector illustrated in some of the details. I think you successfully anthropomorphised a lion unlike I have seen - the "expression" appears pensive and human. Nice to look at for sure!  Congrats.', '2010-01-08 10:36:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5802355, 843201, 19944, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 7. It''s "artsy". I''ve been liking "artsy" more &amp; more lately. It''s something different to look at. Not a deeply saturated landscape (don''t get me wrong, I score them well, too, when they are done well).</td>', 'I gave it a 7. It''s "artsy". I''ve been liking "artsy" more & more lately. It''s something different to look at. Not a deeply saturated landscape (don''t get me wrong, I score them well, too, when they are done well).', '2010-01-08 10:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5802380, 841748, 86218, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on this photo. Being from South Africa myself I apprecite pictures such as this presenting these wild cats in any special way. The face, together with title tells the story of a much bigger scenario playing down here in Africa. It is very special seeing these animals in the wild and free in our parks and hope this can be the case for as long as possible. Also thanks for your compliments. Regards</td>', 'Congratulations on this photo. Being from South Africa myself I apprecite pictures such as this presenting these wild cats in any special way. The face, together with title tells the story of a much bigger scenario playing down here in Africa. It is very special seeing these animals in the wild and free in our parks and hope this can be the case for as long as possible. Also thanks for your compliments. Regards', '2010-01-08 11:12:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5802396, 842207, 90495, '<td valign="top">Too much happening at the same range of contrast for my eyes to target on an interesting point to appreciate. Maybe saturating the reds in the water wheel would give us a point to focus on. The two trees bending inwards from each edge of the image point to nothing interesting for me to want to continue looking there. What I noticed with my own outdoor shots during the winter season was that I attained a kind of abstract look to them because of the many inter-winding lines the branches create. That may be happening here.</td>', 'Too much happening at the same range of contrast for my eyes to target on an interesting point to appreciate. Maybe saturating the reds in the water wheel would give us a point to focus on. The two trees bending inwards from each edge of the image point to nothing interesting for me to want to continue looking there. What I noticed with my own outdoor shots during the winter season was that I attained a kind of abstract look to them because of the many inter-winding lines the branches create. That may be happening here.', '2010-01-08 11:18:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5802399, 842995, 15711, '<td valign="top">I loved this one so much.  It just did something to me with the setting sun creating the orange lines on the eaves of the house to the right.  With the house there, it was so much more than just a seascape.  It gave it an emotion that just a beautiful scene would not.  I think it should have been top 5 for sure.</td>', 'I loved this one so much.  It just did something to me with the setting sun creating the orange lines on the eaves of the house to the right.  With the house there, it was so much more than just a seascape.  It gave it an emotion that just a beautiful scene would not.  I think it should have been top 5 for sure.', '2010-01-08 11:19:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5802416, 839829, 86218, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8 myself and absolutely love this. Congratulations on your ribbon. Thanks so much for your kind comment my pic. I dont think there is anything to choose between most of the pictures posted as all speak very loud on a different level.</td>', 'I gave this an 8 myself and absolutely love this. Congratulations on your ribbon. Thanks so much for your kind comment my pic. I dont think there is anything to choose between most of the pictures posted as all speak very loud on a different level.', '2010-01-08 11:22:34.000000', NULL, 0),
