(5807944, 842601, 22301, '<td valign="top">nice use of filters. I like the light. I think toning down the orange may have helped your score. Eventhough the tobacco filter throws off that color, I am guessing some saw this as overediting. Still I think it is great. Your filters are much cleaner than mine. At this point if I point mine towards the sun, I get speckled artifacts as the sun hits all the scratches. :P</td>', 'nice use of filters. I like the light. I think toning down the orange may have helped your score. Eventhough the tobacco filter throws off that color, I am guessing some saw this as overediting. Still I think it is great. Your filters are much cleaner than mine. At this point if I point mine towards the sun, I get speckled artifacts as the sun hits all the scratches. :P', '2010-01-12 18:09:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5807951, 841701, 72670, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Quigley:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Coley:</b></div><hr/><i> My goodness! where did you get that fine specimen of a model :D<br/> <br/>Max... I said it before It was a blast working with you and Leo. <br/>Top 20 on a free study ! Yea baby! I don''t know if I am happier for you for such a great image and a fine finish;  or for  me for all the calls I will probably get for new modeling gigs<br/>The shot , the lighting and your processing details are amazing. It is so incredible how the lighting changes the shot. <br/>Huge congrats on getting a really awesome image. And once again, thanks for inviting me out to the shoot. It was one of my coolest days of 2009<br/> <br/>Oh I almost forgot  <b>faved</b> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Now this makes this image complete :)<br/> <br/>Thank you Cole for everything. You are AWESOME.<br/> <br/>MAX! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Alright already. Can you guys just kiss and get it over with.<a href="//www.mysmiley.net/free-animal-smileys.php" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.mysmiley.net/imgs/smile/love/love0037.gif'', strrpos(''//www.mysmiley.net/imgs/smile/love/love0037.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.mysmiley.net/imgs/smile/love/love0037.gif"/></a> <a href="//www.mysmiley.net/free-mad-smileys.php" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.mysmiley.net/imgs/smile/happy/happy0009.gif'', strrpos(''//www.mysmiley.net/imgs/smile/happy/happy0009.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.mysmiley.net/imgs/smile/happy/happy0009.gif"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-12 18:15:46.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Quigley: Originally posted by Coley: My goodness! where did you get that fine specimen of a model :D Max... I said it before It was a blast working with you and Leo. Top 20 on a free study ! Yea baby! I don''t know if I am happier for you for such a great image and a fine finish;  or for  me for all the calls I will probably get for new modeling gigsThe shot , the lighting and your processing details are amazing. It is so incredible how the lighting changes the shot. Huge congrats on getting a really awesome image. And once again, thanks for inviting me out to the shoot. It was one of my coolest days of 2009 Oh I almost forgot  faved   Now this makes this image complete :) Thank you Cole for everything. You are AWESOME. MAX!   Alright already. Can you guys just kiss and get it over with. ', '2010-01-12 18:14:16.000000', '2010-01-12 18:15:46.000000', 0),
